WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
1915.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.130
A newspaper page, and a poem
with a question for a title.

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.890
"Who's for the game, the
biggest that's played,

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.770
The red crashing game of a fight?"

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.150
A sports ground.

6
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.090
A whistle.

7
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.620
A row of seats.

8
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.250
One figure stands up, and
walks towards the pitch.

9
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.050
This poem asked young men to
volunteer, by calling war a game.

10
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.240
What does that picture leave out?

11
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.580
In this mission, you'll see why, in 1915,

12
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.310
the army needed poems that persuade.

13
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.540
Conscription only began in 1916.

14
00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.880
You'll count its questions,
and spot its sports words.

15
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.450
And you'll tap along to its
bouncy, song-like rhythm.

16
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.620
Your mission: work out what
calling war a game hides.
